5455:../src/platform/drivers/mss/mss_ethernet_mac/mss_ethernet_mac.c ****  * Auto-detect the PHY's address by attempting to read the PHY identification
5456:../src/platform/drivers/mss/mss_ethernet_mac/mss_ethernet_mac.c ****  * register containing the PHY manufacturer's identifier.
5457:../src/platform/drivers/mss/mss_ethernet_mac/mss_ethernet_mac.c ****  * Attempting to read a PHY register using an incorrect PHY address will result
5458:../src/platform/drivers/mss/mss_ethernet_mac/mss_ethernet_mac.c ****  * in a value with all bits set to one on the MDIO bus. Reading any other value
5459:../src/platform/drivers/mss/mss_ethernet_mac/mss_ethernet_mac.c ****  * means that a PHY responded to the read request, therefore we have found the
5460:../src/platform/drivers/mss/mss_ethernet_mac/mss_ethernet_mac.c ****  * PHY's address.
5461:../src/platform/drivers/mss/mss_ethernet_mac/mss_ethernet_mac.c ****  * This function returns the detected PHY's address or 32 (PHY_ADDRESS_MAX + 1)
5462:../src/platform/drivers/mss/mss_ethernet_mac/mss_ethernet_mac.c ****  * if no PHY is responding.
5463:../src/platform/drivers/mss/mss_ethernet_mac/mss_ethernet_mac.c ****  */
